<InfoLayout title="About the WinGo Learning Lab" description="Learn why this independent educational project explores probability, randomness, and WinGo-style mechanics, and how its examples and sources are checked." eyebrow="A project built around curiosity" lead="We use a familiar number format to make probability easier to explore—and to make the limits of a pattern harder to overlook.">
  <h2>Why this lab exists</h2><p>WinGo Learning Lab is an independent learning project about number classifications, mathematical probability, and statistical thinking. Building the site also provides practical experience with educational publishing and understanding how readers discover and use learning resources.</p><p>The publisher is the WinGo Learning Lab project. We do not claim an operator affiliation, professional certification, or specialist credentials that have not been established.</p>
  <h2>What you can learn here</h2><p>Start with <a href="/what-is-wingo/">the format overview</a>, use the <a href="/wingo-rules/">complete classification table</a>, and work through the <a href="/number-probability/">probability examples</a>. The guides then explain how to interpret streaks, frequencies, and sample sizes.</p><p>The simulator generates local timed or batch experiments, the calculator works through events and ordered sequences, and the randomness demonstration compares sample sizes. Their purpose is to make assumptions visible and calculations inspectable.</p>
  <h2>How we handle evidence</h2><p>Articles distinguish a defined mathematical model from claims about external systems. Worked examples are original; substantive concepts link to sources. The selected classification rules are documented as an example ruleset, rather than presented as universal.</p><p>Constructed data is labeled as illustrative. Future generated runs will identify their local source. A publication date records when a guide was first published in this project, and later substantive revisions will be identified when made.</p>
  <h2>Our limitations</h2><p>We do not verify external game fairness, collect live game results, or establish a predictive advantage. Our uniform model assumes independent draws and equal probabilities. Those assumptions cannot be transferred to another system without evidence.</p><div class="takeaway"><p>There are no real-money deposits, withdrawals, betting, payouts, operator referrals, or guaranteed winning strategies on this site.</p></div>
  <h2>Questions and corrections</h2><p>Clear educational material improves through scrutiny. Public contact details are being finalized; the <a href="/contact/">contact information page</a> records their current status. Until a working channel is available, we do not offer a message form that appears to submit feedback.</p>
</InfoLayout>
